# Events, Jobs, and Queues

- Use domain/application events to decouple secondary effects from core state changes.
- Use queues for non-critical asynchronous work such as notifications, media processing, webhook handling, provider calls, and synchronization jobs where documented.
- Core authoritative state must be committed before asynchronous side effects rely on it.
- Jobs MUST be retry-safe.
- Jobs that can be duplicated MUST be idempotent.
- Configure retry/backoff intentionally; do not rely on unbounded retries.
- Failed jobs must be observable and recoverable.
- Do not put user-facing business decisions exclusively inside an async job if the command needs an immediate authoritative response.
